I completely understand now! You want a classic, full-width **Accordion** style. Like the image you shared, it should have a bold header bar (usually blue), a + or - icon on the right, and the content drops down cleanly below it.
Material UI has a built-in Accordion component that we can style to look exactly like your reference image.
Here is how to implement it:
### 1. Update your Imports
Scroll to the very top of your JournalAuthorization.jsx file. Add the Accordion components and the Plus/Minus icons to your Material UI imports:
```javascript
import {
  // ... your other imports ...
  Accordion,
  AccordionSummary,
  AccordionDetails
} from "@mui/material";
import AddIcon from "@mui/icons-material/Add";
import RemoveIcon from "@mui/icons-material/Remove";

```
### 2. Replace the Description Grid Item
Scroll down to your **View Details Modal**. Find the <Grid item xs={12}> that contains the Description (inside SECTION 1: VOUCHER ORIGIN DETAILS) and replace it entirely with this Accordion block:
```javascript
                        {/* --- ACCORDION FOR DESCRIPTION (MATCHING YOUR DESIGN) --- */}
                        <Grid item xs={12}>
                          <Accordion
                            expanded={isDescExpanded}
                            onChange={(e, expanded) => setIsDescExpanded(expanded)}
                            disableGutters
                            elevation={0}
                            sx={{
                              mt: 1,
                              border: '1px solid #1e3a8a', // Dark blue border
                              borderRadius: '4px !important', 
                              '&:before': { display: 'none' }, // Removes default MUI line
                              overflow: 'hidden'
                            }}
                          >
                            <AccordionSummary
                              // Switches between - and + based on state
                              expandIcon={isDescExpanded ? <RemoveIcon sx={{ color: 'white' }} /> : <AddIcon sx={{ color: 'white' }} />}
                              sx={{
                                backgroundColor: '#1d4ed8', // Bold Blue background like your image
                                color: 'white',
                                minHeight: '48px',
                                '& .MuiAccordionSummary-content': { my: 1.5 },
                                // Stops the + / - icon from spinning upside down
                                '& .MuiAccordionSummary-expandIconWrapper.Mui-expanded': { transform: 'none' } 
                              }}
                            >
                              <Typography variant="subtitle2" fontWeight="bold">
                                View Voucher Description
                              </Typography>
                            </AccordionSummary>
                            
                            <AccordionDetails sx={{ backgroundColor: '#f8fafc', p: 3, borderTop: '1px solid #1e3a8a' }}>
                              <Typography variant="body2" color="text.primary" sx={{ whiteSpace: "pre-wrap", lineHeight: 1.6 }}>
                                {vidDetails.DESCRIPTION || "No description provided."}
                              </Typography>
                            </AccordionDetails>
                          </Accordion>
                        </Grid>

```
### Why this exactly matches your image:
 * **The Bar:** It creates a solid blue header bar (#1d4ed8) with bold white text.
 * **The Icons:** Instead of standard arrows, it explicitly uses the + (AddIcon) when closed, and switches to the - (RemoveIcon) when open, just like your reference.
 * **No Spinning:** I added a specific CSS override (transform: 'none') so the - icon doesn't try to spin upside down when you click it.
 * **The Dropdown:** The content area has a slightly lighter background (#f8fafc) to separate the text from the header, making a 500-word description very easy to read.
